# Build context exclusions.
#
# The Dockerfile copies explicitly (app, .agents, alembic, scripts, and the
# dependency manifests), so nothing here ever reached the image. The cost was
# the context transfer itself: .venv and node_modules alone are ~650MB, sent to
# the daemon on every build, and four services build from this same context.
#
# Keeping .env out is also a standing guard: it is not copied today, but a
# future `COPY . .` would otherwise bake credentials into a layer.
#
# Do NOT add app/services/slides/fonts here. Those CJK fonts are required at
# runtime to render Traditional Chinese slides.

# Python environment and caches
.venv
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache

# Node dependencies: the image runs `npm ci` from package-lock.json instead
node_modules

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Tests and local development artifacts
tests
graphify-out
*.db
*.sqlite3

# Editor and VCS
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea

# Docs
README.md
AGENTIC_WORKFLOW.md
